    <briefdescription>
<para>Creates a quadrilateral finite-element mesh from the input bitmap. The node and element numbering is from 0..n-1; negative numbers identify missing neighbor elements and corresponding model boundary identifiers. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Stephan K. Matthaei </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="author"><para>Stephen G. Roberts </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>1999</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1motivation">
<title>Motivation</title><para>Have a simple procedure to go from a geometry drawn with a pixel-type tool or defined by a processed image, to go to a simple triangular finite-element mesh for CSMP computations. </para>
</sect1>
    </detaileddescription>
